    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF5</id>
      <name>PDS.1#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL be analyzed to determine whether regulatory approval, following realm-specific regulatory rules, is required before the system is made available for general public use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="5"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF6</id>
      <name>PDS.1#02</name>
      <notes>IF realm-specific regulatory approval is determined to be required THEN the system SHALL NOT be presented for general public use until that approval is obtained.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="6"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF7</id>
      <name>PDS.1#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality that predicts, recommends, ranks, classifies, generates content, or initiates actions related to health or wellbeing THEN the system SHALL document the AI functionality's intended purpose, target users, context of use, level of autonomy, and whether the output can influence a health, wellbeing, financial, access, or safety decision; the system SHALL determine whether applicable realm-specific regulatory, privacy, consumer-protection, and medical-device requirements apply.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="7"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF8</id>
      <name>PDS.1#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL maintain an inventory of each AI component, including the component owner, supplier, model or service name, version, intended purpose, deployment location, data categories processed, and whether the component is capable of learning or changing after deployment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="8"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF9</id>
      <name>PDS.1#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide measures to safeguard minors in accordance with applicable regulations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="9"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF10</id>
      <name>PDS.1#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality with a potentially high-impact health or safety use THEN the system SHOULD obtain review by appropriately qualified clinical, safety, privacy, and regulatory personnel before initial deployment and before a material change in intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="10"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF11</id>
      <name>PDS.2 Product Risk Assessment and Mitigation</name>
      <alias>PDS.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category deals with process steps for risk assessment and mitigation for those
 who are developing a new app, or an upgrade to an app, prior to its being deployed to
 consumers.$DE$Degrees of risk should be assessed and mitigated according to the intended use
 of the app. In general, risk management should manage security, privacy, safety, and other
 types of risks such as potential app failure scenarios, events that could lead to undesirable
 outcomes, probability and severity of risk, and mitigations or resolutions. One size does not fit
 all. For example, if apps handle sensitive personal information or give health interpretation or
 advice, higher degrees of risk are involved than for apps that do not collect personal information
 or do not interpret or advise. If some information identified during this step should be disclosed
 to consumers, that is stated in the “Informing Consumers/Users” section.

Related Regulations and Standards:
While mobile computing environments may introduce some specific threats not present in non-mobilecomputing, the principles of risk management
 are the same across environments, so some standards and regulations are cited, even though they are not mobile-centric. Documents (listed
 alphabetically below) were sources of some cMHAFF criteria for risk assessment. Other useful references on risk assessment are listed in the
 Appendix. While some are realm-specific, they have much material that is applicable beyond their countries. Realms are listed in parentheses, if not
 explicit in the title.
 Andalusian Complete list of recommendations on design, use and assessment of health apps:
 http://www.calidadappsalud.com/en/listado-completo-recomendaciones-app-salud/
 • British Standards Institution Publicly Available Specification (PAS) 277:2015 Health and wellness apps – Quality criteria across
 the life cycle – Code of practice: Recommendations andguidance throughout the app’s product development life cycle
 • French Good Practice Guidelines on Health Apps and Smart Devices (Mobile Health or mHealth). https://www.has-
 sante.fr/portail/upload/docs/application/pdf/2017-
 03/dir1/good_practice_guidelines_on_health_apps_and_smart_devices_mobile_health_or_mh ealth.pdf
 • National Institute of Standards and Technology NISTIR 8144 Assessing Threats to MobileDevices &amp; Infrastructure, The
 Mobile Threat Catalogue (USA) https://nccoe.nist.gov/sites/default/files/library/mtc-nistir-8144-draft.pdf (context and background
 information)
 https://pages.nist.gov/mobile-threat-catalogue/application.html#vulnerable-applications (actual catalog of threats, specifically the “Vulnerable
 Application” category, which is the part ofthe threat catalog closest to cMHAFF)
 • Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) Top 10 Mobile Security Risks:
 https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Mobile_Top_10_2016-Top_10 This is focused on appdevelopers, so most of it is pertinent to
 cMHAFF, and for each risk, there are suggested mitigations.
 • OWASP Secure Coding Practices Quick Reference Guide: https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-
 reference-guide/ - This provides resources for developers that can assist in implementing secure coding practices. It is
 recommended that developers adopt secure coding practices so that applications are developed with an emphasis on security vs
 having to apply security measures to protect the application.$EX$While later sections in this standard include specific security and privacy controls to be applied to consumer mobile health apps, all products addressing
health issues, regardless of their type, must be subjected to an overall risk analysis. This risk analysis may uncover the need for additional security controls
over-and-above the conformance statements included in this document. As such, a risk analysis provides an additional layer of considerations such that
conformance statements are not misused as a simple checklist in which it is assumed all security risks have been addressed if an app is in compliance
with the conformance statements in this standard. For an app/product, the risk analysis should be conducted for the target environment(s) where the app
will actually be used by consumers. Because of the diversity of consumers, such a risk analysis is wider ranging and more challenging than a risk analysis
for the development organization’s own environment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF3</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="11"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF12</id>
      <name>PDS.2#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL conform to a product risk assessment and mitigation plan defined by the developer. The plan explicitly determines which risks are addressed through software coding, hardware adaptation, or policy, and which residual risks are accepted by the entity responsible for the system. The developer maintains, reviews, and updates an organizational risk register that includes risks associated with the mobile application.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="12"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF13</id>
      <name>PDS.2#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL extend its product risk assessment and mitigation plan to address AI-specific hazards, including incorrect or fabricated output, unsafe recommendations, biased performance, data drift, privacy leakage, adversarial or malicious inputs, prompt injection, automation bias, over-reliance, and inappropriate use outside the intended context.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="13"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF14</id>
      <name>PDS.2#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL be developed following secure coding practices using an established risk assessment framework.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="14"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF15</id>
      <name>PDS.2#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system collects personally identifiable information THEN the system SHALL be developed in accordance with risk assessment findings regarding the adequate protection of an individual's personally identifiable information (PII), any protected health information (PHI), and information used to access an EHR or PHR, such as logon credentials.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="15"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF16</id>
      <name>PDS.2#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system transmits data to an EHR THEN the system SHALL document failure rates, measurement error rates, software defects, and hardware risks of all types.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="16"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF17</id>
      <name>PDS.2#06</name>
      <notes>IF AI output can influence a high-impact health, safety, or access decision THEN the system SHALL define and test risk controls, escalation paths, user-facing limitations, and a safe fallback behavior for AI unavailability, low confidence, conflicting inputs, or detected unsafe output.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="17"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF18</id>
      <name>PDS.2#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system includes generative AI or an AI agent THEN the system SHALL perform pre-deployment testing for unsafe content, unsupported medical claims, prompt injection, data exfiltration, harmful instructions, and unintended actions appropriate to the system's intended use and consumer population.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="18"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF19</id>
      <name>PDS.2#08</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD be approved through User Acceptance Testing (UAT) conducted by testers who are not part of the formal development team, prior to product launch.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="19"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF20</id>
      <name>PDS.2#09</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD predefine performance, safety, fairness, and usability acceptance thresholds that are proportionate to the intended use and identify the actions taken when a threshold is not met.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="20"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF21</id>
      <name>PDS.2#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD be monitored for, and SHOULD document, conflicts or compatibility issues with other applications, device features such as the camera, or connected devices.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="21"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF22</id>
      <name>PDS.2#11</name>
      <notes>IF the system relies on external supporting infrastructure, such as cloud-based servers, to operate THEN the system SHOULD document measures that ensure the availability of that infrastructure.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="22"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF23</id>
      <name>PDS.2#12</name>
      <notes>The system MAY provide documentation showing that the publisher has adequate resources to continue to develop, maintain, and support the product, such as human resources, finances, intellectual property rights, facilities, equipment, and tools.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="23"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF24</id>
      <name>PDS.2#13</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY use independent evaluators, red-team testing, or external subject-matter experts to challenge assumptions and identify unanticipated AI risks before or after release.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF11</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="24"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF25</id>
      <name>PDS.3 Usability/Accessibility Assessment</name>
      <alias>PDS.3</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about the assessment of usability during the product development cycle, for the intended use by a target audience.$DE$Certain accessibility requirements (usability for users with specific disabilities) are recommended, but the list is not exhaustive. Other
disabilities not mentioned (e.g., cognitive/learning disabilities) should be considered under the umbrella of conformance criterion #1.$EX$The timing of implementation of usability findings can be indicated in functional profiles based on the severity of findings. At a minimum a usability
assessment plan includes information about the timeframe under which remediation will occur.

These conformance statements apply to any type of app addressed in this standard. However, specific usability measures and remediation plans will differ
based on app functionality, intended users, and app platform, and as such this standard does not discuss specific controls; instead, it speaks to a
development process which encourages inclusion and end user satisfaction.

See Appendix: Reference Documents</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF3</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="25"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF26</id>
      <name>PDS.3#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL be assessed against an industry-validated usability assessment tool using subjects who are demographically similar to the intended users (target audience). User types may include, for example, those with motor disabilities, visual impairment, or auditory disabilities.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="26"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF27</id>
      <name>PDS.3#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system displays AI output to consumers THEN the system SHALL assess, with representative intended users, whether consumers can understand that an output is AI-assisted, the output's intended purpose, its material limitations, and the appropriate next step.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="27"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF28</id>
      <name>PDS.3#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD undergo non-functional usability testing that assesses its user-friendliness, performance reliability, and adherence to end-user expectations for the targeted consumer group.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="28"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF29</id>
      <name>PDS.3#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD have a written usability assessment plan that includes known product usability problems and a mitigation plan.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="29"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF30</id>
      <name>PDS.3#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD follow the design and style guide standards established by the platform provider(s) on which it runs, such as Android or iOS.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="30"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF31</id>
      <name>PDS.3#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD avoid excessive data use, minimize data use as far as practicable, and warn the user when high data usage occurs, such as during downloads and updates.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="31"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF32</id>
      <name>PDS.3#07</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD be supported by a requirements analysis that describes the use cases (business scenarios) and intended users for its main functions.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="32"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF33</id>
      <name>PDS.3#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD assess cognitive burden, health literacy, language accessibility, disability access, and the likelihood that interface design could cause users to over-trust or misunderstand AI output.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="33"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF34</id>
      <name>PDS.3#09</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD permit adaptation to the user's specific abilities, needs, or requirements.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="34"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF35</id>
      <name>PDS.3#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide information about its accessibility characteristics in the product description and in the contextual assistance sections of the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="35"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF36</id>
      <name>PDS.3#11</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY provide an accessible explanation mode that uses plain language, translated text, visual aids, or other adaptive presentation methods.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF25</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="36"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF37</id>
      <name>PDS.4 Customer/Technical Support</name>
      <alias>PDS.4</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. Information as to how to access customer support, and channels of support (e.g., voice, email, PDS.4 NC
 text, Twitter) SHALL clearly be stated within the app's Terms of Use and as a feature accessible
 from within the app.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF3</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="37"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF38</id>
      <name>PDS.4#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL clearly state how to access customer support and the available support channels, such as voice, email, text, or social media, within its Terms of Use and as a feature accessible from within the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="38"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF39</id>
      <name>PDS.4#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL make customer support accessible prior to the establishment of a user account, so that a user can raise questions about the Privacy Policy or Terms of Use before deciding to use the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="39"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF40</id>
      <name>PDS.4#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide customer support in the language(s) in which it is published.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="40"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF41</id>
      <name>PDS.4#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL give attribution to any open source code library or copyrighted code used in its development, within its Terms of Use or in documentation available from within the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="41"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF42</id>
      <name>PDS.4#05</name>
      <notes>IF a support request involves accessing, disclosing, or changing customer data THEN the system SHALL verify the identity of the customer and the customer's data access rights before any customer data is disclosed or changed.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="42"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF43</id>
      <name>PDS.4#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide responses to customer support queries that directly address the stated problem or issue within two business days. An acknowledgement that a query has been received, without further action, is not sufficient.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="43"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF44</id>
      <name>PDS.4#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL provide consumers with a clear mechanism to report suspected inaccurate, harmful, biased, misleading, or privacy-impacting AI output, and the system SHALL route reports into a documented investigation and remediation process.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="44"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF45</id>
      <name>PDS.4#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality that can influence a high-impact health or safety decision THEN the system SHOULD provide an expedited path to human support or an appropriate safety resource when a consumer reports a potentially serious AI-related issue.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="45"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF46</id>
      <name>PDS.4#09</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide consumers with aggregated satisfaction ratings relevant to the customer support terms and conditions, as appropriate.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="46"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF47</id>
      <name>PDS.4#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide a frequently asked questions (FAQ) resource where users can find answers to common questions.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF37</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="47"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF48</id>
      <name>Product Implementation</name>
      <alias>PIM</alias>
      <notes>$OV$Apps are frequently marketed and downloaded through platform-specific “app stores.” Before an app can be housed within an app store, it must meet requirements set by the app store host. The app store is one primary source of product information for consumers to decide whether they want to install the app. In some realms, apps may also be obtained through an app registry.$EX$$AC$</notes>
      <stereotype>Section</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF</parentId>
      <tag name="ID" value="2"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF49</id>
      <name>PIM.1 Product Information</name>
      <alias>PIM.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about providing information about the product to consumers and also other parties (e.g., governments, consumer or provider
organizations) who have interest in potential purchase, use, endorsement, or recommendation of apps. The experience of installing an app begins at an
app store and completes on a user device. See also the Conditions and Agreements section of this specification for guidance regarding Conditions and
Agreements that usually appear as part of the app store experience. cMHAFF does not specify exactly how or where product information is conveyed,
e.g., app store, web site, online help.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Header</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF48</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="49"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF50</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1 General Information</name>
      <alias>PIM.1.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF49</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="50"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF51</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL include in its product description the main functionality, the intended use, the intended (target) audience, and the potential use of the user's personal data by the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="51"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF52</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide screen shots that accurately depict the screens of the current version of the product.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="52"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF53</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide product information before it is used by the consumer, to help the consumer decide whether the system is suitable.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="53"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF54</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD clearly state in its product description the human languages it supports.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="54"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF55</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide information about the publisher (persons or organizations) and SHOULD provide mechanisms for communicating with the publisher.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="55"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF56</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD disclose its sources of funding and any possible conflicts of interest, such as use of the system incentivizing the user to buy products or services from the publisher.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="56"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF57</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL state in its product description whether it uses AI functionality, what that functionality does, what data it uses, and whether AI output is used to inform health-related information, recommendations, or decisions.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="57"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF58</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses an external AI service THEN the system SHALL state in its product description the limitations of its AI functionality, including the populations, conditions, or contexts for which the AI function was not evaluated.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="58"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF59</id>
      <name>PIM.1.1#09</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD disclose the provider or organization accountable for the AI-enabled feature and provide a mechanism to contact that organization about safety, privacy, or performance concerns.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF50</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="59"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF60</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2 Payment</name>
      <alias>PIM.1.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. The payment amount for the app, if any, SHALL be clearly noted according to app store rules. PIM.1 NC$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF49</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="60"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF61</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL clearly state the payment amount for the system, if any, in accordance with app store rules.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF60</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="61"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF62</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system requires or offers optional payments after download THEN the system SHALL clearly state this in its app store description, together with the amount of payment required and the results of such in-app payments, for example that payment of a certain amount produces an advertisement-free experience. The system SHALL also state the impact of not making payments, such as limited functionality.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF60</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="62"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF63</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2#03</name>
      <notes>IF the user is being signed up for a set period of recurring payments THEN the system SHALL notify the user.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF60</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="63"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF64</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2#04</name>
      <notes>IF access to an AI-enabled feature requires payment THEN the system SHALL disclose the price, subscription terms, feature limitations, and whether the paid AI feature changes the type, amount, or frequency of consumer data processing.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF60</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="64"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF65</id>
      <name>PIM.1.2#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system provides safety-related information through an AI-enabled feature THEN the system SHOULD NOT condition access to essential safety notices, risk disclosures, or the ability to report an unsafe AI output on purchase of a premium feature.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF60</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="65"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF66</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3 Evidence/Credentials</name>
      <alias>PIM.1.3</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. IF the app provides health recommendations, the scientific degree of evidence and the types PIM.1 NC
 and dates of sources used (e.g., clinical practice guidelines and protocols, peer-reviewed
 articles, professionals and organizations with their credentials) that guided the app content
 SHALL be disclosed.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF49</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="66"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF67</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system provides health recommendations THEN the system SHALL disclose the scientific degree of evidence and the types and dates of the sources that guided its content, such as clinical practice guidelines and protocols, peer-reviewed articles, and professionals and organizations with their credentials.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="67"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF68</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI for health-related recommendations, interpretation, or decision support THEN the system SHALL disclose the evidence basis, evaluation method, intended population, validation setting, material performance measures, and known limitations of the AI function in a level of detail appropriate to the system's intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="68"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF69</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD reference or provide sufficient information for consumers to easily access the supporting evidence for review, which may include clinical, social, technical, and other domains of potential relevance.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="69"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF70</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD provide a plain-language summary of what evidence supports the AI function, what is not known, and how the function should and should not be used.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="70"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF71</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system provides human or automated interpretation of health-related content THEN the system SHALL disclose the credentials of the qualified health professionals involved, and/or SHALL document the algorithms and the associated testing plans and reports.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="71"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF72</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL identify the date and version of the AI model or service used for the consumer-facing function, or provide another stable mechanism by which an evaluator can determine the version in use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="72"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF73</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#07</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD identify in its product description the health professionals and credentials of those who worked on the system, or at minimum the professional organization that made, reviewed, endorsed, or sponsored it.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="73"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF74</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#08</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD show the date of its last update and describe the changes from the previous release, such as revisions due to new scientific evidence.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="74"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF75</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#09</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD declare the degree of admission of liability, that is the publisher's acceptance or disclaimer of responsibility, regarding the selection and use of its content.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="75"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF76</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#10</name>
      <notes>The system MAY include in its product description data related to reliability and validity testing or population research results.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="76"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF77</id>
      <name>PIM.1.3#11</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY publish independent evaluation results, peer-reviewed studies, or an assessment report that describes performance and limitations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF66</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="77"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF78</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4 Limitations and Warnings</name>
      <alias>PIM.1.4</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. Contraindications, potential risks and limitations of use SHALL be documented. For example, PIM.1 NC
 environmental or patient conditions under which apps or connected devices may be unreliable
 (e.g., tattoos that impact optical sensors; avoid usage when pregnant; avoid usage outside a
 temperature range).$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF49</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="78"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF79</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL document contraindications, potential risks, and limitations of use, for example environmental or patient conditions under which the system or connected devices may be unreliable, such as tattoos that affect optical sensors, use during pregnancy, or use outside a specified temperature range.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="79"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF80</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system provides health recommendations, such as general guidelines, THEN the system SHALL disclose the potential risks to patient safety and their mitigations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="80"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF81</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#03</name>
      <notes>IF AI output can reasonably lead a consumer to take an urgent health or safety action THEN the system SHALL provide a safe, context-appropriate next-step instruction and a clear statement of any emergency or clinician-contact limitations of the AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="81"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF82</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system collects de-identified data THEN the system SHOULD provide documentation of how the data is de-identified and of its current and planned secondary uses.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="82"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF83</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system offers health advice, such as specific and personal health decision support, THEN the system SHOULD state that use of the system does not replace the provider-patient relationship or the recommendation, opinion, or diagnosis of a health professional.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="83"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF84</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD warn users of updates that are caused by possible errors in functionality, in health-related information, or in any other sensitive data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="84"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF85</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system has collected personal health information THEN the system SHALL guarantee the integrity of data stored across its different versions.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="85"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF86</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL disclose material AI limitations, including known unvalidated populations or contexts, input-quality assumptions, situations in which the output may be unreliable, and the possibility that the output may be incorrect, incomplete, or unsuitable for the individual user.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="86"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF87</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#09</name>
      <notes>IF the system presents AI-generated health content, advice, or a recommendation THEN the system SHALL clearly distinguish AI-generated content from human-authored or clinician-reviewed content and SHALL NOT represent AI output as a diagnosis, treatment order, or professional judgment unless the system is authorized and validated for that use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="87"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF88</id>
      <name>PIM.1.4#10</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD display a just-in-time warning when the user's context, available data, or request appears to be outside the validated or intended use of the AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF78</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="88"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF89</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5 Technical Details</name>
      <alias>PIM.1.5</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. IF the user can enter personal health information into the app, it SHALL clearly disclose PIM.1 NC
 whether or not data validity checking is done, and document or reference the evidence for such
 validity checking.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF49</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="89"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF90</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#01</name>
      <notes>IF the user can enter personal health information into the system THEN the system SHALL clearly disclose whether data validity checking is performed, and SHALL document or reference the evidence for that validity checking.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="90"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF91</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system collects or receives quantitative data THEN the system SHALL document and justify the precision, that is the accuracy and granularity, of measurements such as physical activity or physiological data from connected devices, as appropriate for its intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="91"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF92</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL maintain technical documentation sufficient for an assessor to determine the AI function's model or service type, version, intended use, input data categories, output types, data transformations, dependency services, and known operational constraints.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="92"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF93</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#04</name>
      <notes>IF AI output is derived from health data THEN the system SHALL document the data-quality checks, missing-data behavior, input validity constraints, and known measurement or transcription limitations that can affect the AI output.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="93"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF94</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system hosts personal health information THEN the system SHALL document backup and recovery procedures that comply with applicable regulatory requirements.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="94"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF95</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#06</name>
      <notes>IF personal health data are imported into or exported from the system THEN the system SHALL document its data import and export functions, including the ability to convert to standard formats.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="95"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF96</id>
      <name>PIM.1.5#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD make a consumer-accessible technical summary or model card available without requiring disclosure of proprietary source code or trade secrets.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF89</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="96"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF97</id>
      <name>PIM.2 Launch App and Establish User Account</name>
      <alias>PIM.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. A user SHALL be able to review the app's Terms of Use before personal data about the user PIM.2 NC
 is collected and used.$DE$$EX$• Use Case A: Knowing who the user is, in an absolute sense, is not needed as data is not being sent to any external data set. Primarily, account
 controls are in place to ensure the same person is using the app each time. For this walking app, possession of a smartphone may be sufficient to
 allow someone to use it without any additional need for authentication or need to set up a unique user ID and password to access the app.
 • Use Case B: Knowing the user’s absolute identity is not needed but minimal account controls (e.g., user ID and password) should be established
 as the app will allow information to be sent to an existing data set, and these data sets will need some ability to be linked, in part showing evidence
 an individual has control over both the app data and a right to access the existing data set.
 • Use Case C: requires more rigorous identity proofing as data will be both sent to an EHR and interactions initiated by a physician result in information
 being pushed to the app. Identity proofing can occur within the app itself, or in the use of pre-existing identity credentials (e.g., patient portal
 credentials for the entity controlling the EHR) to establish identity.

 3. App Use
 Statement Overview: This section addresses functionalities and considerations to be addressed while the user is operating
 the app.</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF48</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="97"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF98</id>
      <name>PIM.2#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL permit a user to review its Terms of Use before personal data about the user is collected and used.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="98"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF99</id>
      <name>PIM.2#02</name>
      <notes>IF account data, content, or device data will be transmitted to an AI component THEN the system SHALL inform the user, before the first such transmission, what categories of data will be processed by the AI component, whether a third party receives the data, and the purposes, retention, and applicable data-use choices.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="99"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF100</id>
      <name>PIM.2#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system creates user accounts THEN the system SHALL log the user's acceptance of its Terms of Use before a user account is authorized. See APU.9 for audit log record creation.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="100"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF101</id>
      <name>PIM.2#04</name>
      <notes>IF the user is allowed to use pre-existing account credentials from an Identity Provider (IdP) to access the system THEN the system SHALL inform the user, before the user chooses to use those credentials, (a) what attribute information associated with the pre-existing credentials will be used by the system, and (b) what data is communicated back to the IdP at the time of account creation and at each subsequent user authentication.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="101"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF102</id>
      <name>PIM.2#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD collect no more than the minimum necessary amount of a user's personally identifiable information (PII) for the purpose of establishing an account, that is, information necessary to authenticate the user, provide customer support, or affect the system's logic.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="102"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF103</id>
      <name>PIM.2#06</name>
      <notes>IF user data will be used to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or otherwise improve an AI model THEN the system SHALL obtain the user's permission before the first transmission of account data, user content, or device data to an AI component, and SHALL identify the recipient, the purpose, and whether the data may be retained.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="103"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF104</id>
      <name>PIM.2#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system offers optional AI features THEN the system SHOULD allow a user to enable or disable optional AI features separately from unrelated App functions when technically feasible and consistent with the intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF97</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="104"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF105</id>
      <name>App Use</name>
      <alias>APU</alias>
      <notes>$OV$This section addresses functionalities and considerations to be addressed while the user is operating
the app.$EX$$AC$</notes>
      <stereotype>Section</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF</parentId>
      <tag name="ID" value="3"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF106</id>
      <name>APU.1 Authentication</name>
      <alias>APU.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about the system protecting against unauthorized access (e.g., by persons other than the consumer).$DE$The functionality of an app, its sponsorship, and linkages to external data sources all affect the security, privacy and data controls which are
established to ensure safe and effective use. In this section, conformance criteria point to issues which can be addressed through a range of options, and
as such implementers should consider not only the conformance criteria but the discussion regarding applicability to the exemplary use cases.$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="106"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF107</id>
      <name>APU.1#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL authenticate the identity of a user prior to any access to PHI or PII.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="107"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF108</id>
      <name>APU.1#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL communicate the method of authentication to the user when an account is established.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="108"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF109</id>
      <name>APU.1#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL authorize the user to access a feature before that feature or any associated PHI or PII is displayed. Authorization may be internal to the system or derived from an external source.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="109"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF110</id>
      <name>APU.1#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL terminate, at the request of a user, such that subsequent access to PHI or PII requires a new, successful authentication attempt.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="110"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF111</id>
      <name>APU.1#05</name>
      <notes>IF another external health IT system, such as an EHR, is a system actor THEN the system SHALL verify a subject's association with their real-world identity, establishing that the subject is who they claim to be (identity proofing).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="111"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF112</id>
      <name>APU.1#06</name>
      <notes>IF an EHR is a system actor THEN the system SHALL ensure that the EHR authorizes the user's access to those system features that are supported by data provided by, or written to, the EHR.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="112"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF113</id>
      <name>APU.1#07</name>
      <notes>IF PII or PHI are displayed THEN the system SHALL terminate, or make PHI and PII invisible, after a period of user inactivity as described in its Terms of Use. This feature is sometimes called inactivity timeout, session timeout, or automatic logoff. The decision to include this feature is made as part of the overall risk analysis regarding the sensitivity of the data provided by or through the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="113"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF114</id>
      <name>APU.1#08</name>
      <notes>IF passwords are stored on the device THEN the system SHALL encrypt those passwords and SHALL NOT display them as plaintext.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="114"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF115</id>
      <name>APU.1#09</name>
      <notes>IF access to an account exposes Protected Health Information (PHI) or PII THEN the system SHALL give the user the option to use strong authentication methods, such as multi-factor authentication or biometrics, in addition to passwords. Before the user selects this option, the system clearly describes or demonstrates the authentication mechanism. This capability may apply to the system itself and to the pairing of the system with a device.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="115"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF116</id>
      <name>APU.1#10</name>
      <notes>IF an AI component can access PHI, PII, credentials, or an external system on behalf of a user THEN the system SHALL ensure that the AI component receives only the least-privileged, time-limited access necessary for the authorized task and SHALL prevent the AI component from exposing authentication secrets, tokens, or credentials in consumer-visible output or logs.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="116"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF117</id>
      <name>APU.1#11</name>
      <notes>IF an AI-enabled function can execute an external action or disclose new data THEN the system SHOULD require re-authentication or another strong confirmation before the action is completed when the risk assessment identifies a meaningful risk of harm, disclosure, or irreversible change.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF106</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="117"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF118</id>
      <name>APU.2 User Authorizations</name>
      <alias>APU.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about personal data collection and use, including access to device features, being understood and explicitly
 authorized (consented to) by the users of the app.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="118"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF119</id>
      <name>APU.2#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL use smartphone functionality and data sources only when essential to perform its specific functions. These include, but are not limited to, location services, camera, microphone, accelerometer and other sensors, contact lists, and calendars.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="119"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF120</id>
      <name>APU.2#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL ask the user for permission before using selected smartphone functions and data sources for the first time. The user can individually specify permissions for each function, data source, and user tracking activity controlled by the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="120"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF121</id>
      <name>APU.2#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL ask the user for permission to transmit data before exporting data from the smartphone or from any device integrated with the smartphone, explaining what data is being transmitted, to which recipients, and for what purposes, such as to the supplier's servers, for backups, or for large-scale data analysis. Permission is requested before the first potential transmission of data. Permission is requested again the first time any additional data elements are sent to an external data source where permission had previously been given for a smaller set of data. Permission is not requested at every transmission if the scope of exported data remains unchanged.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="121"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF122</id>
      <name>APU.2#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system sends PII, PHI, user-entered content, device data, or derived data to an external AI provider THEN the system SHALL obtain permission before the first transfer and clearly identify the recipient, purpose, data categories, retention approach, and whether the provider may use the data to train or improve a model.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="122"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF123</id>
      <name>APU.2#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system requests permission to use data it generated after that data is de-identified THEN the system SHALL inform the account holder who would have access to the de-identified data and for what purpose.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="123"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF124</id>
      <name>APU.2#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system requests permission to use data it generated after that data is de-identified THEN the system SHALL inform the account holder of the possibility that de-identified data can potentially be re-identified, and of the steps the sponsor takes to prevent re-identification.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="124"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF125</id>
      <name>APU.2#07</name>
      <notes>IF the user gives permission for data generated by the system to be de-identified and used THEN the system SHALL de-identify that data following, at minimum, realm-specific rules, such as HIPAA Safe Harbor in the USA.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="125"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF126</id>
      <name>APU.2#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system supports in-app payments THEN the system SHALL NOT trigger in-app payments in a way that can expose healthcare-related information to payment organizations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="126"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF127</id>
      <name>APU.2#09</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses in-app advertising THEN the system SHALL disclose to the user the potential use of PHI or PII to personalize advertisements, and SHALL give the user the opportunity to consent or decline.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="127"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF128</id>
      <name>APU.2#10</name>
      <notes>IF the system requests to share data with social networks THEN the system SHALL provide the user with options to select which types of data will be shared, and SHALL inform the user of the potential consequences of the secondary use and sharing of that data outside the system's control. The system SHALL NOT commence data sharing with social networks until the user has consented.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="128"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF129</id>
      <name>APU.2#11</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD permit a user to allow some, but not all, requested data to be exported from a smartphone or associated device, and SHOULD inform the user how limiting the data affects its functionality.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="129"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF130</id>
      <name>APU.2#12</name>
      <notes>IF a user denies a permission requested by the system THEN the system SHOULD inform the user of the consequence of not granting the permission and SHOULD give the user a further opportunity to grant it.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="130"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF131</id>
      <name>APU.2#13</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL provide a mechanism for a user to withdraw optional AI-related permissions and SHALL explain the effect of withdrawal on App functionality and on future AI data processing.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="131"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF132</id>
      <name>APU.2#14</name>
      <notes>IF the system offers more than one AI feature THEN the system MAY allow a user to make granular choices by AI feature, data type, or purpose, such as an AI coaching feature, document summarization, or model-improvement use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF118</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="132"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF133</id>
      <name>APU.3 Pairing or Syncing User Accounts with Devices and Data Repositories</name>
      <alias>APU.3</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about consumer verification of all devices to which they wish to pair or sync data.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="133"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF134</id>
      <name>APU.3#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL ensure that the user has successfully authenticated and has an active session before an external device is paired to an account.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="134"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF135</id>
      <name>APU.3#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL display a screen that asks the user to confirm that the device will collect information about a specific, named person, before a device is paired with the system to collect information about that individual. The person may be the account holder or a proxy subject of the account holder.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="135"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF136</id>
      <name>APU.3#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide a utility function that permits the person who paired a device with an individual to un-pair the device and the individual.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="136"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF137</id>
      <name>APU.3#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL state what data will be collected by the device and how that data is used, before a device is paired with the system to collect information about a specific individual. This statement may include a link to an informational page giving details about data collection and use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="137"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF138</id>
      <name>APU.3#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses device or repository data as input to AI functionality THEN the system SHALL state, before a device or repository is paired or synced, whether data from that device or repository will be used as input to AI functionality and for what purpose.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="138"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF139</id>
      <name>APU.3#06</name>
      <notes>IF data for more than one person can be collected by the system and device pair THEN the system SHALL ask the account holder to confirm the person for whom the device will collect data, before data is collected and transmitted.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="139"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF140</id>
      <name>APU.3#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system includes a syncing option, such as the same data synchronized across smartphone and tablet devices, THEN the system SHALL provide the user with the option to consent to the syncing process.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="140"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF141</id>
      <name>APU.3#08</name>
      <notes>IF AI output depends on data from a paired device or repository THEN the system SHOULD detect or flag material missing, stale, implausible, or mis-associated inputs before presenting an AI output that relies on those inputs.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF133</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="141"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF142</id>
      <name>APU.4 Security for Data at Rest and in Transport</name>
      <alias>APU.4</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about providing assurance that the consumer’s stored data is secure, regardless of whether it is stored on the consumer’s
 devices or elsewhere (e.g., in cloud-based servers for an app). It also provides assurance that consumer data is secure when it is moved between the
 consumer’s device(s) and other locations.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="142"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF143</id>
      <name>APU.4#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL store PHI and PII held on a smartphone as encrypted values.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="143"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF144</id>
      <name>APU.4#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL store PHI and PII held on any external server as encrypted values.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="144"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF145</id>
      <name>APU.4#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL permit the account holder to delete information collected through the system, including data generated by an associated device, unless that PHI or PII has been transmitted to a data set maintained by a health plan or health provider.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="145"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF146</id>
      <name>APU.4#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL improve or upgrade its encryption ciphers and suites to match evolving best practices while it is actively being developed and maintained, that is, while it is not being sunset.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="146"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF147</id>
      <name>APU.4#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system contains PHI or PII THEN the system SHALL transmit PHI and PII between itself and an external data source, including data generated through an associated device, as encrypted values.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="147"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF148</id>
      <name>APU.4#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses an AI component THEN the system SHALL protect consumer data, prompts, retrieved content, model inputs, model outputs, API keys, and access tokens used by the AI component using security controls proportionate to the data sensitivity and deployment architecture.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="148"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF149</id>
      <name>APU.4#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses a third-party AI service THEN the system SHALL assess and document the security and privacy controls of the third-party AI service, including data isolation, retention, access controls, incident notification, and the provider's use of consumer data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="149"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF150</id>
      <name>APU.4#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system includes generative AI or retrieval-augmented generation THEN the system SHOULD implement technical controls to reduce prompt injection, unauthorized retrieval, data exfiltration, and cross-user data exposure.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF142</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="150"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF151</id>
      <name>APU.5 Data Authenticity, Provenance, and Associated Metadata</name>
      <alias>APU.5</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about providing assurance that consumer data is secure when it is moved between the consumer’s device(s) and other
 locations. This category is about the attribution of sources of data (provenance) and assurance of data authenticity.$DE$Related Regulations and Standards:
The following are examples of standards for data provenance. Even though they are specific to the FHIR and CDA standards respectively, the principles
 and data elements -- for recording entities and processes involved in producing or delivering a resource (data) – may be applicable.
 • FHIR Provenance Resource http://www.hl7.org/FHIR/provenance.html
 • HL7 CDA® R2 Implementation Guide: Data Provenance, Release 1 - US Realm
 http://www.hl7.org/implement/standards/product_brief.cfm?product_id=420
 • ISO 21089 Health Informatics – Trusted End-to-End Information Flows. https://www.iso.org/standard/35645.html Offers a guide to trusted
 end-to-end information flow for health(care) records and to the key trace points and audit events in the electronic entity/act record lifecycle
 (from point of record origination to each ultimate point of record access/use).$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="151"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF152</id>
      <name>APU.5#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL conform to best practices for data authenticity, provenance, and associated metadata.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="152"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF153</id>
      <name>APU.5#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system creates an AI-derived output that is stored, displayed, exported, or exchanged THEN the system SHALL label the output as AI-derived and retain provenance sufficient to identify the source data references, model or service identifier and version, time of generation, and whether a human reviewed or modified the output.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="153"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF154</id>
      <name>APU.5#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system itself originates data, as defined in ISO 21089, THEN the system SHALL provide the customer with the option to review, irreversibly destroy, reject, or discard that data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="154"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF155</id>
      <name>APU.5#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system only receives data as a pass-through and cannot store data THEN the system SHALL provide the customer with a review option that displays the data prior to executing the pass-through, including the option to irreversibly stop and block the pass-through.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="155"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF156</id>
      <name>APU.5#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system receives data and stores it THEN the system SHOULD provide the customer with a review option that permits only appending data or free-text comments to the received data as author, while preserving the original received data intact with its original provenance. The user may comment that data are erroneous but does not have the option to delete the original data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="156"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF157</id>
      <name>APU.5#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system displays AI output derived from consumer or device data THEN the system SHALL preserve or reference the original source data without overwriting it and SHALL distinguish AI interpretation, summarization, prediction, or generated content from the original data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="157"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF158</id>
      <name>APU.5#07</name>
      <notes>IF the AI function produces a meaningful confidence, uncertainty, or quality signal THEN the system SHOULD preserve and present the signal in a manner appropriate to the intended user and SHALL NOT present a confidence value as a guarantee of correctness.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF151</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="158"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF159</id>
      <name>APU.6 Data Exchange and Interoperability</name>
      <alias>APU.6</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category applies only if an app exchanges data with other devices, health apps, and/or HIT systems. If so, there are applicable
 standards for data format, vocabulary, and transport, to increase interoperability and ease of connection.$DE$Related Regulations and Standards:
• Direct Project Applicability Statement for Secure Health Transport
 https://www.healthit.gov/policy-researchers-implementers/direct-project
 • HL7 Consolidated CDA
 • HL7 FHIR STU. http://www.hl7.org/FHIR/index.html
 • SMART ON FHIR. https://smarthealthit.org/
 • http://www.hl7.org/implement/standards/product_brief.cfm?product_id=379
 • IEEE 10073 Personal Health Data Standards https://standards.ieee.org/develop/wg/PHD.html
 • “MedMij” information Exchange standards for Personal Health Environment https://www.medmij.nl (Netherlands) Includes HL7 Health
 Clinical Information models (HCIM), which provide context for discrete clinical data (e.g., systolic blood pressure); the standard is being used
 in the Netherlands.$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="159"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF160</id>
      <name>APU.6#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges discrete clinical data THEN the system SHALL use standard terminologies, such as SNOMED CT or LOINC.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="160"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF161</id>
      <name>APU.6#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges discrete clinical data THEN the system SHALL use standard format and content, such as HL7 FHIR, SMART on FHIR, HL7 Consolidated CDA, or Detailed Clinical Models (HL7 CIMI).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="161"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF162</id>
      <name>APU.6#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges AI-derived data with another device, app, repository, or HIT system THEN the system SHALL identify AI-derived information as such in the exchanged content and SHALL include available provenance, source-data, model-version, and human-review metadata so recipients can distinguish it from verified clinical observations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="162"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF163</id>
      <name>APU.6#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges discrete clinical data with devices THEN the system SHOULD use standard format and content, such as IEEE 11073.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="163"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF164</id>
      <name>APU.6#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges unstructured data THEN the system SHOULD use standard or commonly accepted formats, such as HL7 CDA or PDF.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="164"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF165</id>
      <name>APU.6#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges AI-generated narrative or summary content THEN the system SHALL distinguish AI-generated narrative from source records and SHALL avoid transmitting the narrative as a verified clinical fact unless it has been reviewed and authenticated according to the receiving system's policy.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="165"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF166</id>
      <name>APU.6#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system collects personal health information THEN the system SHOULD allow that data to be imported into or exported from the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="166"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF167</id>
      <name>APU.6#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system exchanges AI-derived data THEN the system SHOULD use applicable interoperable provenance and annotation mechanisms, such as HL7 FHIR Provenance or a realm-appropriate equivalent, when those mechanisms are available to the receiving system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF159</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="167"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF168</id>
      <name>APU.7 Notifications and Alerts</name>
      <alias>APU.7</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category applies only if an app exchanges data with other devices, health apps, and/or HIT systems. If so, there are applicable
 standards for data format, vocabulary, and transport, to increase interoperability and ease of connection.$DE$$EX$In the realm of alerts and notifications, the following table proposed suggested standardized (generic)terms in the left column, with mappings to the
 leading two platforms in the middle columns, and comments in the right column. The platform-specific definitions have been derived from web
 sources,with preference given to information from the creators of the platforms (Apple, Google). Note: the mapping cannot be made an exact 1:1. In
 some cases, the platform-specific term may be more precise(e.g., subtypes) than the generic term, but we do not require a generic equivalent for
 every platform- specific term. In other cases, there may be substantial similarity of concepts across platforms, but not identical behavior, and
 certainly not identical appearance.

 Despite the proposed granularity of these terms, that does not mean that there need to be separatecMHAFF conformance requirements for each
 type, but at least the opportunity is there if the need arises. In particular, there may be different conformance requirements for “alerts” vs other
 types ofnotifications.

