 Hierarchy

 • Message (overarching term)
 o Content Message (e.g., HL7 v2, C-CDA payload, FHIR resource) – out of the scope for this set of definitions.
 o Notification (overarching term)
  Alert (requires user action, whereas all other types of notifications do not require it,though they may allow it)
  Persistent notification
  Temporary notification
  Emergency Notification (government, outside app control)</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="168"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF169</id>
      <name>APU.7#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL require opt-in consent from the account holder before sending notifications and alerts.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="169"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF170</id>
      <name>APU.7#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL inform the account holder of both the content and the channel, such as SMS, push notification, or email, of the notification or alert that is consented to.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="170"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF171</id>
      <name>APU.7#03</name>
      <notes>IF an alert, notification, or message is generated or prioritized by AI THEN the system SHALL identify the message as AI-generated or AI-prioritized when that information is material to the user's interpretation or action.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="171"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF172</id>
      <name>APU.7#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the account holder with the ability to change consent decisions about notifications and alerts through settings available on the device on which the system was downloaded.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="172"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF173</id>
      <name>APU.7#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide notifications and alerts that contain the least amount of information necessary for the recipient to take a focused action.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="173"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF174</id>
      <name>APU.7#06</name>
      <notes>IF alerts notify the user of conditions that are abnormal, exceptional, or determined to be out of range THEN the system SHALL document or reference the sources (evidence base) of the formulas and algorithms on which those alerts and notifications are based.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="174"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF175</id>
      <name>APU.7#07</name>
      <notes>IF an AI-generated alert advises a health or safety action THEN the system SHALL ensure that the alert's triggering logic, evidence basis, validation scope, and safe escalation instructions are documented and appropriate to the system's intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="175"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF176</id>
      <name>APU.7#08</name>
      <notes>IF permitted by the account holder and agreed to by the recipients THEN the system SHOULD provide the ability to send notifications and alerts to the account holder and to another person or entity.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="176"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF177</id>
      <name>APU.7#09</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide alerts that notify the user of potential faults that could cause inconvenience or harm, such as low battery alerts.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="177"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF178</id>
      <name>APU.7#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD notify the user in the case of external interruptions or delays, such as loss of network connection, a database problem, or a lengthy operation.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="178"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF179</id>
      <name>APU.7#11</name>
      <notes>IF the system can detect AI uncertainty, out-of-distribution input, or unavailable supporting data THEN the system SHOULD suppress, downgrade, or qualify the AI-generated alert when the risk assessment indicates that the underlying output may be unreliable.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="179"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF180</id>
      <name>APU.7#12</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI to personalize notification timing or content THEN the system MAY allow the account holder to control the personalization settings and the categories of data used for personalization.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF168</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="180"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF181</id>
      <name>APU.8 Product Upgrades</name>
      <alias>APU.8</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. The App SHALL respect operating system level permissions concerning automatic product APU.8 NC
 updates.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="181"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF182</id>
      <name>APU.8#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL respect operating system level permissions concerning automatic product updates.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="182"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF183</id>
      <name>APU.8#02</name>
      <notes>IF an updated version of the system includes updated Terms of Use THEN the system SHALL present the updated Terms of Use to the account holder for acceptance before the updated version may be used. Significant changes to the terms and conditions are highlighted, and a link to the full set of updated Terms of Use is available.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="183"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF184</id>
      <name>APU.8#03</name>
      <notes>IF automatic updates are not enabled THEN the system SHALL prompt the user when a new version is available.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="184"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF185</id>
      <name>APU.8#04</name>
      <notes>IF an account holder elects not to install a new version THEN the system SHALL inform the user of the consequences of not installing it, including information about support limitations for the older version.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="185"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF186</id>
      <name>APU.8#05</name>
      <notes>IF a new version increases what information is exposed by alerts THEN the system SHALL require the user to consent to the information being exposed, and SHALL clearly highlight the changes to the exposed information when that consent is given.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="186"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF187</id>
      <name>APU.8#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL treat a material change to an AI model, prompt, retrieval source, training data, inference service, or decision threshold as a controlled product change and SHALL document the change, risk assessment, validation, approval, and rollback plan before deployment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="187"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF188</id>
      <name>APU.8#07</name>
      <notes>IF an AI change materially affects data use, intended use, performance, or consumer-facing risk THEN the system SHALL notify affected users before or at deployment, explain the material change in understandable terms, and obtain updated permission when the change expands personal-data use or another consent-relevant practice.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="188"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF189</id>
      <name>APU.8#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD maintain the ability to suspend or roll back an AI component without requiring removal of unrelated App functionality when a material safety, privacy, or performance issue is detected.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF181</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="189"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF190</id>
      <name>APU.9 Audit</name>
      <alias>APU.9</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about auditing, which is a mechanism for user and system accountability. Important events, such as logins and access to
 particular functions and data, are recorded and can be used to detect instances of non-compliant behavior and to facilitate detection of improper
 creation, access, modification, and deletion of personal health information. Any information technology including consumer health apps should follow
 best practices in managing an audit trail. The audit trail should maintain a record of users who have accessed what data, from where, and when. Audit
 logs should also record any attempts to access the system from an unauthorized terminal; expired usernames or passwords that try to access the
 system, unusual numbers of authentication attempts, and violations of an organizations security policy.$DE$Related Regulations and Standards:
• Integrating the Healthcare Enterprise (IHE) Audit Trail and Node Authentication (ATNA)
 Integration Profile. https://www.ihe.net/Technical_Frameworks/#IT This IHE profile references
 the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) RFC 3881 Audit Record standard
 https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc3881/
 • HL7 EHR Records Management and Evidentiary Support Functional Profile, Release 1
 (RMES) ( http://www.hl7.org/implement/standards/product_brief.cfm?product_id=86 ) Provides
 functions in an EHR system that can help an organization maintain a legal record for business
 and disclosure purposes.$EX$Every consumer mobile health app needs an audit strategy, which includes what data will be generated for audit, who will be able to access audit records,
 the location where audit data is stored, the length of time audit information will be stored, and any ability to delete audit data. Audit for security events is
 highly dependent on the nature of the app itself; audit requirements will differ significantly based on app sponsorship (e.g., sponsor is a HIPAA entity or a
 commercial non-covered entity), the need for user authentication, and if data generated through an app is accessible by consumers, clinicians, or both.</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF105</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="190"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF191</id>
      <name>APU.9#01</name>
      <notes>IF user authentication is required to access the system THEN the system SHALL generate an audit record of authentication attempts, both successful and unsuccessful.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="191"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF192</id>
      <name>APU.9#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL generate an audit record of user permissions to access, or the revocation of access to, smartphone or tablet device capabilities used by the system, such as camera or location services.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="192"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF193</id>
      <name>APU.9#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses external devices or data sources for data collection THEN the system SHALL generate an audit record of the pairing of a device or data repository external to the system that supplies data used by the system.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="193"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF194</id>
      <name>APU.9#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system allows the export of data to a data repository external to the system THEN the system SHALL generate an audit record of any export of data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="194"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF195</id>
      <name>APU.9#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL generate an audit record for AI processing events that is sufficient to reconstruct the event without unnecessarily retaining sensitive prompt content, including the user or system actor, AI component and version, time, authorization context, input source references, output disposition, and any resulting action.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="195"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF196</id>
      <name>APU.9#06</name>
      <notes>IF an AI output is overridden, corrected, reported as unsafe, or leads to a safety incident THEN the system SHALL record the event, the applicable model version, the type of issue, investigation outcome, and corrective action, subject to applicable privacy and retention requirements.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="196"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF197</id>
      <name>APU.9#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD provide an authorized consumer or evaluator with a comprehensible history of the AI outputs and material actions associated with that consumer when doing so is safe and technically feasible.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF190</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="197"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF198</id>
      <name>App Service Termination</name>
      <alias>AST</alias>
      <notes>$OV$Health apps may be used indefinitely or for a finite period of time and will consequently require the ability to terminate services with the app.Disuse may happen when a health condition improves, a new health habit is established, when motivation to use the app wanes, or when
 the user determines a different app better meets their needs. Procedures for how data continues to be retained and used after account closure must be
 clear and understandable and give the app user options for relocation of their data to a new data repository.$EX$$AC$</notes>
      <stereotype>Section</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF</parentId>
      <tag name="ID" value="4"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF199</id>
      <name>AST.1 App and Data Removal</name>
      <alias>AST.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$$DE$Related Regulations and Standards:
• European Union Privacy Code of Conduct on Mobile Health apps
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-single-market/en/privacy-code-conduct-mobile-health-apps$EX$Data download should be in a standard or at least nonproprietary format (e.g., CSV, XML, JSON) that
can be manipulated by off-the-shelf tooling. The format should be selected appropriate to the data being
downloaded.</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF198</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="199"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF200</id>
      <name>AST.1#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the account holder with the ability to remove the system from a mobile device at any time.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="200"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF201</id>
      <name>AST.1#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL inform the account holder of the consequences of removing it from a smartphone, such as loss of locally stored data, and SHALL give the account holder an opportunity to confirm the removal before it occurs.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="201"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF202</id>
      <name>AST.1#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the account holder with the ability to close an associated account or data store.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="202"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF203</id>
      <name>AST.1#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL inform the account holder of the consequences of deleting the account and SHALL give an opportunity to confirm closing the account before it is closed.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="203"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF204</id>
      <name>AST.1#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL inform the account holder that data that was part of the account may have been transmitted to other systems outside the account itself and may persist. For example, where the user collects device data in the system and transmits that data to an EHR which stores it as patient-generated health data, the user is informed that deleting the account may not delete the data now held in the EHR.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="204"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF205</id>
      <name>AST.1#06</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses consumer data in AI processing THEN the system SHALL stop future AI processing and future model-improvement use of that account's data when the account is closed, unless another documented legal basis applies, and SHALL describe any retained data required for legal, safety, or security reasons.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="205"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF206</id>
      <name>AST.1#07</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the account holder with the ability to download data generated by the account holder, or by a proxy subject of the account holder, to a data set under the full control of the account holder (data portability), before an account is closed.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="206"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF207</id>
      <name>AST.1#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system provides consumer data portability THEN the system SHOULD include AI-generated or AI-derived data in the export and preserve available provenance, source-data references, model version, and human-review status.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="207"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF208</id>
      <name>AST.1#09</name>
      <notes>IF the device on which the system is installed permits remote or external access to device data THEN the system SHALL provide the ability for any PHI or PII stored on the device to be wiped remotely by the account holder, without deleting the account related to the wiped data.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="208"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF209</id>
      <name>AST.1#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD set and communicate to the user clear criteria regarding the deletion of data, including automatic deletion if the user has not used the system for a specified period.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="209"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF210</id>
      <name>AST.1#11</name>
      <notes>IF the system stores prompts, retrieval caches, embeddings, AI outputs, or AI audit data linked to an account THEN the system SHALL delete, de-identify, or otherwise render unusable the prompts, retrieval caches, embeddings, AI outputs, and AI audit data linked to the account, or SHALL state which categories are retained, for what purpose, and for how long, when an account is closed.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF199</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="210"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF211</id>
      <name>AST.2 Permitted Uses of Data Post Account Closure</name>
      <alias>AST.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about what is done with consumers’ data if they close their account (terminate use of the app).$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF198</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="211"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF212</id>
      <name>AST.2#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL NOT disclose data associated with a closed account to any new persons or entities, including data that has been de-identified.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF211</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="212"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF213</id>
      <name>AST.2#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL offer the consumer the option to decide what to do with their data, such as keeping it or deleting it.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF211</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="213"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF214</id>
      <name>AST.2#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system has closed an account THEN the system SHALL NOT use data associated with the closed account for future AI training, fine-tuning, evaluation, or model improvement unless the consumer previously gave specific permission or another applicable legal basis is documented.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF211</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="214"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF215</id>
      <name>AST.2#04</name>
      <notes>IF consumer data has already been used to train or fine-tune an AI model THEN the system SHOULD explain whether and how the account-closure choice affects already-trained models, derived artifacts, backups, and future model releases, including any technical limits on removing an individual's contribution from a deployed model.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF211</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="215"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF216</id>
      <name>Conditions and Agreements</name>
      <alias>CNA</alias>
      <notes>$OV$This section of cMHAFF deals with nonfunctional, and usually nontechnical, aspects of mobile health apps. While not traditionally in scope for
 HIT standards oriented at large or small enterprise organizations, it is a very important and distinctive characteristic of apps targeted at consumers.Since one goal of cMHAFF is consumer protection, including their privacy and security, guidance in the area of “Conditions and Agreements”
 (CnA) is offered. CnA is not a formal or legal term, but an umbrella under which can be grouped various expressions of conditions that consumers to which
 are asked to agree
 before they start using a mobile health app. These may be called “Terms and Conditions,” “Terms of
 Use,” “Terms of Service,” “End User License Agreement (EULA),” and similar concepts. Typically, CnA are displayed and consumers are asked to click
 buttons to agree to terms, when they interact with “App Stores” (a generic term including wherever a consumer downloads a mobile health app). In addition
 to what the consumer agrees to, CnA may also commit the app supplier to certain behaviors or restrictions. While cMHAFF does not prescribe what these
 CnA must include, it provides guidance as to items that are important to disclose. In that respect, there is some precedent in the ONC 2015 Edition
 Certification, which contains disclosure and transparency requirements for EHR developers, e.g., about pricing and services that are not included in the
 base software.$EX$$AC$</notes>
      <stereotype>Section</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF</parentId>
      <tag name="ID" value="5"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF217</id>
      <name>CNA.1 Specifications for Conditions and Agreements</name>
      <alias>CNA.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$1. The App developer SHALL, before download, allow the potential user to easily access the CNA.1 C
 Apps Terms of Use. This may be accomplished through a link in the app description in the
 relevant app store.$DE$Related Regulations and Standards:
• Federal Trade Commission: How to Make Disclosures in Digital Advertising, March 2013
 https://www.ftc.gov/sites/default/files/attachments/press-releases/ftc-staff-revises-online-
 advertising-disclosure-guidelines/130312dotcomdisclosures.pdf (USA). Explains how to make
 disclosures clear and conspicuous to avoid deception and takes into account the expanding use
 of smartphones.
•$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF216</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="217"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF218</id>
      <name>CNA.1#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL allow a potential user to easily access its Terms of Use before download. This may be accomplished through a link in the product description in the relevant app store.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="218"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF219</id>
      <name>CNA.1#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL allow a potential user to easily access its Privacy Policy before download. This may be accomplished through a link in the product description in the app store.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="219"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF220</id>
      <name>CNA.1#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL describe in its Terms of Use the AI functionality used, the data processed by it, the role of automated decision-making, and the consumer's options regarding that processing.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="220"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF221</id>
      <name>CNA.1#04</name>
      <notes>IF consumer data may be used to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or improve an AI model THEN the system SHALL describe that purpose distinctly and SHALL NOT rely on a vague statement such as 'service improvement' as the sole disclosure of the AI data use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="221"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF222</id>
      <name>CNA.1#05</name>
      <notes>IF rewards are given for participation THEN the system SHALL clearly disclose all conditions and time limitations governing those rewards. These include, but are not limited to, how activity is tracked, how promptly rewards are fulfilled, whether rewards can expire or be withdrawn, whether and how rewards can be transferred to another person, and whether rewards can be accumulated into larger rewards.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="222"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF223</id>
      <name>CNA.1#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability for the consumer to indicate that they acknowledge and understand its functionality.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="223"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF224</id>
      <name>CNA.1#07</name>
      <notes>IF the system includes in-app payments THEN the system SHALL disclose what is included as base functionality without payment and what functionality requires additional payment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="224"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF225</id>
      <name>CNA.1#08</name>
      <notes>IF the system permits in-app payments THEN the system SHALL clearly state the benefits of paying for a service or feature in a manner that allows an account holder to make an informed decision about making or declining an in-app payment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="225"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF226</id>
      <name>CNA.1#09</name>
      <notes>IF access to the system is by subscription THEN the system SHALL clearly state the requirements for cancelling a subscription in the Conditions and Agreements.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="226"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF227</id>
      <name>CNA.1#10</name>
      <notes>IF the system requires an additional charge to upgrade THEN the system SHALL clearly state in the Conditions and Agreements the upgrade charges, the amount of advance warning for upgrades, and the length of support for the old version if it is not upgraded.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="227"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF228</id>
      <name>CNA.1#11</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL disclose the use of advertising mechanisms, distinguish advertisements from its content, and provide ways to deactivate or skip advertisements.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="228"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF229</id>
      <name>CNA.1#12</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide a means for a user to access its Privacy Policy at any time during use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="229"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF230</id>
      <name>CNA.1#13</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD provide a concise, consumer-friendly AI summary in addition to full legal terms, covering what the AI does, its limits, what data it uses, when a person reviews it, and how the user can turn optional features off.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="230"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF231</id>
      <name>CNA.1#14</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY provide just-in-time disclosures or short interactive explanations at the point where an AI feature is first used.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF217</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="231"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF</id>
      <name>CMHAFF</name>
      <alias/>
      <stereotype>HL7-FM</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <tag name="PrioritiesDescription" value=""/>
      <tag name="Type" value="Domain"/>
      <tag name="Rationale" value="&lt;memo>"/>
      <tag name="Version" value="1.0"/>
      <tag name="Scope" value="&lt;memo>"/>
      <tag name="LanguageTag" value=""/>
      <tag name="PrioritiesDefinition" value="&lt;memo>"/>
      <tag name="ConformanceClause" value="&lt;memo>"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF233</id>
      <name>AIG.1 AI Applicability, Intended Use, and Inventory</name>
      <alias>AIG.1</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category establishes whether AI functionality is present, what each AI function is intended to do, for whom, with what autonomy, and what inventory the developer maintains about it. It is the entry point for the remaining criteria in this section.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="233"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF234</id>
      <name>AIG.1#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL determine whether each AI function is consumer-facing, clinician-facing, background-only, or agentic; whether it can affect health, safety, privacy, access, cost, or care; and which cMHAFF AI criteria apply to that function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF233</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="234"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF235</id>
      <name>AIG.1#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL define the intended use, intended user, target population, expected inputs, expected outputs, prohibited uses, and foreseeable misuse for each AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF233</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="235"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF236</id>
      <name>AIG.1#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD classify AI functions using a documented risk tier that considers the sensitivity of data, level of autonomy, likelihood of harm, severity of harm, and the presence of human review.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF233</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="236"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF237</id>
      <name>AIG.2 AI Governance and Accountability</name>
      <alias>AIG.2</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about named, documented responsibility for each AI function across its lifecycle, and about the approval gates that make that responsibility operational rather than aspirational.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="237"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF238</id>
      <name>AIG.2#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL designate an accountable organization and accountable role for the governance, safety, privacy, performance monitoring, and retirement of each AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF237</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="238"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF239</id>
      <name>AIG.2#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL establish documented approval criteria for AI design, validation, deployment, material change, suspension, and retirement, including the circumstances requiring review by safety, clinical, privacy, security, or legal personnel.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF237</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="239"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF240</id>
      <name>AIG.2#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY establish an independent advisory group or external review mechanism for AI functions with elevated safety, equity, or consumer-protection risk.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF237</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="240"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF241</id>
      <name>AIG.3 AI Data Governance and Data Rights</name>
      <alias>AIG.3</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about the data used to develop, evaluate, retrieve for, and operate AI functionality: its source, the rights held over it, the purposes it may serve, how long it is retained, and what controls apply when a third party processes it.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="241"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF242</id>
      <name>AIG.3#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL document the source, rights, quality controls, intended use, retention, and permitted processing of data used to develop, test, evaluate, retrieve for, or operate the AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF241</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="242"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF243</id>
      <name>AIG.3#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses consumer data for AI processing THEN the system SHALL use consumer data for AI purposes only within the disclosed and authorized purpose, and SHALL apply data minimization, access control, and retention limits appropriate to the data sensitivity.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF241</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="243"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF244</id>
      <name>AIG.3#03</name>
      <notes>IF a third-party AI provider processes PHI, PII, or sensitive consumer content THEN the system SHALL establish and document controls for data isolation, subprocessor use, data retention, training prohibition or authorization, security incidents, and deletion or return of data when the service relationship ends.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF241</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="244"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF245</id>
      <name>AIG.3#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD assess the risk that de-identified, aggregated, embedded, or derived data could be re-identified, inferred, or exposed through the AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF241</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="245"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF246</id>
      <name>AIG.3#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY use privacy-preserving techniques, such as de-identification, minimization, secure enclaves, or federated approaches, when they are appropriate to the intended use and risk assessment.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF241</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="246"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF247</id>
      <name>AIG.4 AI Validation, Performance, and Equity</name>
      <alias>AIG.4</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about evaluating an AI function against its documented context of use before deployment, documenting what was and was not evaluated, and establishing whether performance differs materially across the populations the application serves.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="247"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF248</id>
      <name>AIG.4#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL evaluate the AI function, before deployment, for performance, safety, reliability, and usability in the documented context of use and against pre-specified acceptance criteria.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF247</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="248"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF249</id>
      <name>AIG.4#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality that can affect health, safety, access, or material wellbeing THEN the system SHALL evaluate whether performance differs materially across relevant subgroups, including populations defined by age, sex, language, disability, geography, device type, health condition, or other factors relevant to the intended use, and SHALL address identified unacceptable disparities.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF247</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="249"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF250</id>
      <name>AIG.4#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL document the performance measures used, their limitations, the evaluation dataset characteristics, and the conditions under which the AI function was not evaluated or did not meet acceptance criteria.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF247</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="250"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF251</id>
      <name>AIG.4#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD obtain external or independent validation when the risk assessment identifies elevated potential for health, safety, equity, or consumer-protection harm.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF247</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="251"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF252</id>
      <name>AIG.4#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY publish a performance dashboard or public validation summary that identifies the intended use, relevant performance metrics, and limitations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF247</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="252"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF253</id>
      <name>AIG.5 Human Factors, Explainability, and Human Oversight</name>
      <alias>AIG.5</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about what the consumer can see, correct, question, and override. It covers review and escalation pathways before high-impact or irreversible actions, correction of faulty input data, and explanation at a level appropriate to the consumer and the risk of the intended use.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="253"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF254</id>
      <name>AIG.5#01</name>
      <notes>IF an AI function can influence a high-impact health, safety, access, or financial decision THEN the system SHALL provide a risk-appropriate human or consumer review, correction, override, or escalation pathway before an irreversible or high-impact action is taken, unless a documented exception is required for immediate safety and is permitted by applicable rules.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF253</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="254"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF255</id>
      <name>AIG.5#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL enable a consumer to view or correct material input data that the consumer provided or that the system attributes to the consumer when incorrect input could materially affect the AI output.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF253</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="255"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF256</id>
      <name>AIG.5#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system displays AI output THEN the system SHOULD provide a meaningful explanation of the primary factors, data limitations, or evidence sources relevant to the output, at a level appropriate to the consumer and the risk of the intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF253</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="256"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF257</id>
      <name>AIG.5#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY offer alternative explanation formats, such as plain-language summaries, detailed technical explanations, visual context, or translated content.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF253</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="257"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF258</id>
      <name>AIG.6 Generative AI and AI Agent Safety</name>
      <alias>AIG.6</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category applies only where the application generates content or acts on a user's behalf. Generative and agentic functions introduce content, prompt-injection, and action risks that deterministic application logic does not.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="258"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF259</id>
      <name>AIG.6#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses generative AI THEN the system SHALL implement controls proportionate to the intended use to reduce generation of unsafe, misleading, fabricated, discriminatory, or privacy-violating content and SHALL define the actions taken when such content is detected.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF258</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="259"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF260</id>
      <name>AIG.6#02</name>
      <notes>IF generative AI is used to provide health-related factual content or recommendations THEN the system SHALL ground the output in curated, version-controlled, and appropriately sourced content or another documented evidence process suitable to the intended use, and SHALL identify when the system cannot verify the requested information.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF258</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="260"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF261</id>
      <name>AIG.6#03</name>
      <notes>IF an AI agent can execute external actions, write to a record, transmit data, purchase a service, or otherwise act on behalf of a user THEN the system SHALL limit the agent's authorized actions, present the action and material consequences to the user before execution when appropriate, and maintain an auditable record of the action request, authorization, execution, and result.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF258</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="261"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF262</id>
      <name>AIG.6#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses generative AI or an AI agent THEN the system SHOULD conduct scenario-based testing for prompt injection, jailbreaks, unsafe advice, disallowed actions, privacy leakage, and escalation to safe human or non-AI resources.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF258</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="262"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF263</id>
      <name>AIG.6#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses generative AI THEN the system MAY use retrieval-augmented generation or other grounding methods when they improve evidence traceability, provided the system validates source quality, freshness, and access controls.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF258</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="263"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF264</id>
      <name>AIG.7 Monitoring, Change Control, and Incident Management</name>
      <alias>AIG.7</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category is about what happens after deployment: monitoring for performance degradation, drift and misuse; pre-defined thresholds and decision authorities for responding; and handling incidents that affect consumer safety, privacy, or performance. AI behavior can change without a conventional application release.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="264"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF265</id>
      <name>AIG.7#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL monitor the AI function after deployment for material performance degradation, data drift, misuse, unexpected outputs, safety events, privacy events, and differences from the validated intended use.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF264</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="265"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF266</id>
      <name>AIG.7#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHALL define and document thresholds and decision authorities for investigation, consumer communication, limitation, suspension, rollback, corrective action, and retirement of an AI function.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF264</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="266"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF267</id>
      <name>AIG.7#03</name>
      <notes>IF a material AI incident affects consumer safety, privacy, or performance THEN the system SHALL investigate the incident, preserve evidence, assess affected consumers and data, implement corrective action, and make notifications required by applicable laws, contracts, or safety protocols.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF264</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="267"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF268</id>
      <name>AIG.7#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system SHOULD periodically review real-world performance across relevant populations and use cases to identify emerging performance or equity concerns.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF264</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="268"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF269</id>
      <name>AIG.7#05</name>
      <notes>IF the system uses AI functionality THEN the system MAY publish de-identified, aggregate post-deployment monitoring summaries when doing so does not create security, privacy, or proprietary risk.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF264</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="269"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF270</id>
      <name>AIG.8 AI Supplier and Third-Party Component Management</name>
      <alias>AIG.8</alias>
      <notes>$ST$This category applies where AI functionality depends on an external model, service, dataset, tool, or content source. Supplier-side changes can alter performance or data handling without any change to the application itself.$DE$$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF232</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="270"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF271</id>
      <name>AIG.8#01</name>
      <notes>IF the system relies on an external AI model, service, dataset, tool, or content source THEN the system SHALL assess and document the supplier's role, applicable data flows, security and privacy controls, model or service versioning, change-notice practices, incident-notification obligations, and ability to support an audit or investigation.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF270</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="271"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF272</id>
      <name>AIG.8#02</name>
      <notes>IF the system relies on an external AI component THEN the system SHALL maintain the ability to identify the component version in use and to suspend or replace the component when a material safety, privacy, security, or performance issue is identified.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF270</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="272"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF273</id>
      <name>AIG.8#03</name>
      <notes>IF the system relies on an external AI component THEN the system SHOULD evaluate material supplier changes before enabling them for consumers and SHOULD retain evidence of the review.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF270</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="273"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF274</id>
      <name>AIG.8#04</name>
      <notes>IF the system relies on an external AI component THEN the system MAY maintain an exit, substitution, or data-portability plan for critical AI suppliers to reduce dependency and continuity risk.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF270</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="274"/>
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY"/>
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y"/>
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N"/>
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator"/>
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>CMHAFF232</id>
      <name>AI Functionality and Governance</name>
      <alias>AIG</alias>
      <notes>$OV$This section addresses artificial intelligence functionality in consumer mobile health applications: governance, transparency, privacy, security, data provenance, user control, safety, monitoring, and accountability.

Consistent with cMHAFF's design as a horizontal, realm-agnostic framework, this section specifies cross-cutting consumer safeguards that apply wherever AI functionality is present. Disease-specific clinical validity, diagnosis and treatment claims, performance targets, threshold logic, and realm-specific regulatory obligations remain the province of implementation guides and realm or domain profiles.

Every criterion in this section is conditional on the presence of AI functionality. An application that uses no AI functionality has no obligations under this section. AIG.1 establishes that applicability determination and is the entry point for the rest.Applicability is determined by the AI questions proposed for the cMHAFF decision table: whether the app uses AI to predict, classify, recommend, rank, summarize, generate content, or act on a consumer's behalf; whether AI output can influence a health, safety, access, or financial decision; whether generative AI, retrieval-augmented generation, or an AI agent is used; whether PII, PHI, device data, or user content is sent to a third-party AI service; whether the AI function can change after deployment; and whether AI-derived data is exchanged with an EHR, PHR, device, payer, or other system.

Design inputs: NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0); NIST AI 600-1 Generative AI Profile; FDA Good Machine Learning Practice Guiding Principles; FDA Transparency for Machine Learning-Enabled Medical Devices; FDA AI-Enabled Device Software Functions lifecycle guidance; FDA Predetermined Change Control Plan guidance; FDA Digital Health and AI Glossary. These are design inputs, not asserted legal requirements; realm-specific law and regulation take precedence.$EX$$AC$</notes>
      <stereotype>Section</stereotype>
      <type>Package</type>
      <parentId>CMHAFF</parentId>
      <tag name="ID" value="6"/>
    </object>
  </objects>
